{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You shall not test YHWH your Elohim.</b> Scripture warns that a person should not test the Holy One, blessed be He, saying, 'I will serve HaShem and see whether my affairs prosper through His service' — for it is not fitting to serve Him with conditional service, but rather one should resolve in his heart to serve Him with complete service out of love, whether he prospers or does not prosper. For there are times when troubles and misfortunes befall a person even as he serves HaShem, and he must believe that all is in the just judgment of the Judge of righteousness, and that the one judged is a fool who does not comprehend His ways; therefore it is not fitting to test Him. And it says, 'as you tested at Massah,' for so Israel tested Him at Rephidim in the matter of seeking water, and they said (Exodus 17), 'Is YHWH in our midst or not?' And it is written (ibid.), 'because of the strife of the children of Israel and because of their testing YHWH.' The test was: if He gives them water they will follow Him, and if He does not give, they will not follow Him — and this is the sense of במסה in the language of knowledge, for on account of this He called the name of the place Massah and Merivah. And Scripture says (Psalms 78), 'And they tested El in their heart.' Now this was conditional service in which there is no completeness at all, and therefore Scripture forbade testing here. But we find that testing was permitted in the matter of charity, and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: 'except for this,' as it is said (Malachi 3), 'Bring all the tithe into the storehouse, that there may be food in My house, and test Me now in this, said YHWH of Hosts.' And so Solomon said (Proverbs 3), 'Honor YHWH with your substance,' and so forth, 'and your vats will burst with must.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:10.429975459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}